Z||000000||Smokin87||01-18-2001||08:14 PM||||i posted this earlier, but didnt get a reply.  how do you remove the ground effects.  i am fixing the piece under the drivers side door, and i have removed all visible rivits (10 total) and 2 screws, but it still wont come off.  is there something im missing, or am i just retarted.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||01-18-2001||08:27 PM||||Have you removed the 4 or 5 rivits in the door jamb under the covers yet? In either event, there are locking tabs that go into the upper ground effects the you'll need to get down and eye-ball the you need to depress in the center of each (with a screw driver) in order to remove the panel.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Notchit||01-18-2001||10:33 PM||||but BE careful when you are removing the tabs along the side, depress them with a screwdriver and push towards the floor, if you press too hard *SNAP* which is what i did    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>good luck!<P>------------------<BR>Seein Red<BR>'85 Fiero GT<BR>ICQ#: 56708070<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Outside_side2(sml2).jpg"> <BR>_________________________||||reg||4
